: Types:

: b = boolean
: s = DcMstr (default/recommended string type)
: dcs = DcStr
: letters = string in StageL character set (capital A-Z, slash, colon, space, newline, brace, dot)
: v/ = verb (an additional type is required)
: l/ = list (a primitive type is required)
: void (does not have a return value)
: never (does not return)
: view: a struct: (source_id: u32, offset: u64, len: u64)
: cursor: a mutable reader positioned at pos: u64 within a view (I guess this would be a (pos: u64, view: view))
: result: Err or Ok(type)
: option: None or Some(type)
: primitive types:
: u8
: i32
: u32
: i64
: u64
: i128
: u128
: int (arbitrary-precision)
: rat (arbitrary-precision: struct (num: int, den: int))
: dc (in effect a u128, but typed)

: tests specify input value and expected return values

: Identifiers are not case-sensitive.

: Newline or brace ends a parameter list

: Dot (or semicolon, which is normalized to dot in intermediate) ends a statement

: conditionals use: if cond ifTrue ifFalse

: loops use: while cond verb

: list iteration can use: foreach list verb

: "this" is a reserved identifier for use by the current element in foreach loops

: typing is strict and there is no automatic coercion


: Leading LET is implicit and can be omitted
let v/b/zl s/in
    test works with zero length string
        in s:
        out 1
    test works with nonzero length string
        in s:a
        out 0
    eq 0 len s/in

let v/s/getFormatImportSetting s/a s/b
    s:UNIMPLEMENTED

v/s/dcGetMappingToFormat s/a s/b
    s:UNIMPLEMENTED

v/b/nne n/a n/b
    : number not equal to (this is a comment; any bytes allowed until nl)
    false

: brace ends a parameter list
let v/b/sneOne s/a s/b } false

: semicolon desugars to a dot
let v/b/sneTwo s/a s/b } false.
: does the same thing
let v/b/sneThree s/a s/b } false;

: this returns s/b if s/a is empty, else s/a
let v/b/default s/a s/b / if zl s/a / s/b s/a

: this returns a verb named "default"
let v/v/b/default s/a s/b / /default s/a s/b / if zl s/a / s/b s/a

: written more nicely
v/v/b/default s/a s/b
    /default s/a s/b / if zl s/a / s/b s/a

v/l/u32/appendU32 lu32/a lu32/b
    : append one list to another
    : UNIMPLEMENTED
    test works
        in l:0 1 l:2 3
        out l:0 1 2 3
    l:0 3 2 1

v/s/getTargetLanguageForDctCodeToText
    new s/targetLanguage getFormatImportSetting s:codetotext s:language
    if zl s/targetLanguage : getEnvCodeLanguage : s/targetLanguage

v/l/dcaFromElad s/in
    : UNIMPLEMENTED
    l:0 1 2 3

v/l/push l/in n/toPush
    : UNIMPLEMENTED

v/l/convertElementAndAppend n/e s/targetLanguage l/converted
    new s/temp dcGetMappingToFormat n/e s/targetLanguage
    if ne 0 len s/temp } lappend l/res dcaFromElad s/temp } push l/res n/currentDc
    : Alternatively, can indent arguments for readability (this is still one logical line). Only one level of indentation allowed.
    if
        ne 0 len s/temp }
        lappend l/res dcaFromElad s/temp }
        push l/res n/currentDc

e:l/dctCodeToText l/in
    new l/res
    new s/targetLanguage getTargetLanguageForDctCodeToText
    each l/in set l/res convertElementAndAppend /e s/targetLanguage l/res
    l/res

: Identifiers are ASCII case-insensitive. Typing is strict; there is no automatic coercion.
: Types: b, s (DcMstr), dcs (DcStr), letters, u8, i32, u32, i64, u64, i128, u128, int, rat, dc, view, cursor.
: b literals: true, false. There is no unspecified numeric type n.
: l/T is a list of T. v/T[A,B] is a verb taking A,B and returning T; v/T[] takes no arguments.
: void has no value; never does not return normally.
: result/T: tagged union Err(error) or Ok(T). option/T: tagged union None or Some(T).
: Constructor expressions: result/T:err ERROR, result/T:ok VALUE, option/T:none, option/T:some VALUE.
: error variants include overflow, division_by_zero, invalid_denominator; literals use error:NAME.
: OPEN: Define extensible error payloads, result/option matching, and explicit error propagation syntax.
: rat contains num:int and den:int; require den nonzero, positive, and coprime to num. Zero is normalized to 0/1.
: makeRat NUM DEN returns result/rat; zero denominator produces Err(invalid_denominator).
: Arithmetic operations return result/T. Fixed-width integer overflow produces Err(overflow), never wrapping.
: Division by zero produces Err(division_by_zero); an unrepresentable quotient produces Err(overflow).
: Errors are ordinary result values, not automatic returns from the enclosing verb.
: OPEN: Define integer division rounding, remainder signs, shifts, conversions, and allocation-failure behavior.
: view contains source_id:u32, offset:u64, len:u64; cursor contains pos:u64 and a view.
: OPEN: Define source lifetimes, checked view bounds, cursor ownership, and enforce pos <= len.
: String length counts Dcs, not bytes or Unicode code points; len returns u64. List length counts elements.
: OPEN: Define string equality, lossless non-Unicode Dc literals, and the precise letters alphabet.
: Opening braces are prohibited outside strings/comments. Block and list openings are implicit.
: Declarations: [let] v/RETURN/name TYPE/parameter ... HEADER_END BODY.
: HEADER_END is newline for an indented body, or } for an inline body containing one statement.
: Indentation delimits declaration bodies. Dot ends statements; semicolon normalizes to dot outside literals/comments.
: The final statement supplies a body's value. A void body may be empty; a value-returning body may not.
: Prefix calls have fixed arity; collect verb signatures before parsing bodies. Overloading is prohibited.
: /name refers to a verb; call /name ARGUMENTS invokes it. Direct calls use name ARGUMENTS.
: if CONDITION THEN ELSE takes expressions, requires b, and evaluates only the selected branch.
: Branch result types must agree, except never is compatible with either branch's type.
: do introduces an implicit expression block, terminated by }; its final statement supplies its value.
: while CONDITION BODY reevaluates both expressions as needed; CONDITION must return b, BODY void.
: foreach LIST BODY evaluates LIST once and BODY for each element; BODY must return void.
: foreach provides read-only T/this. Nested foreach is prohibited until an explicit element-binding syntax is defined.
: break exits the nearest loop; continue starts its next iteration. Neither accepts a label or level count.
: Both have type never at their occurrence and cannot cross a callback/verb boundary.
: Bindings are in scope throughout their block, including before their declaration; shadowing is prohibited.
: new TYPE/name VALUE declares and initializes a mutable binding; set TYPE/name VALUE mutates it and returns void.
: Reads or writes before initialization are rejected. Verb declarations are available throughout their block.
: Callbacks inherit enclosing scope and capture shared bindings; mutations are visible to all users of those bindings.
: Captured bindings remain alive after their declaring invocation returns.
: OPEN: Specify definite-initialization checks across callbacks and the WASM representation of captured bindings.
: Strings use s:"..." or dcs:"..." with JSON escapes; typed numbers use u32:0.
: List literals start with l/T: and end with }; elements are expressions, such as l/u32: u32:0 u32:1 }.
: eq/ne compare same-typed values. concat returns a new list; foreach iterates a snapshot.
: A colon at the first nonblank position starts a comment through newline.
: test LABEL has indented in/out lines: in supplies arguments; out supplies one expected value.
: OPEN: Specify ABI, ownership, recursion limits, and WASM lowering for wide integers, int, rat, and strings.
: unimplemented MESSAGE is a development-only never-returning stub, not recoverable error handling.
let v/b/zl s/in
    test works with zero length string
        in s:""
        out true
    test works with nonzero length string
        in s:"a"
        out false
    eq u64:0 len s/in.
v/result/i64/addChecked i64/a i64/b } add i64/a i64/b.
let v/s/getFormatImportSetting s/a s/b } unimplemented s:"Import settings".
v/s/dcGetMappingToFormat dc/a s/b } unimplemented s:"Dc mapping".
v/b/nne i64/a i64/b } ne i64/a i64/b.
let v/b/sneOne s/a s/b } ne s/a s/b.
let v/b/sneTwo s/a s/b } ne s/a s/b.
let v/b/sneThree s/a s/b } ne s/a s/b;
let v/s/default s/a s/b } if zl s/a s/b s/a.

: The creator returns a verb accepting two strings
v/v/s/makeDefault s/a s/b } }
    v/s/chooseDefault s/a s/b }
        if zl s/a s/b s/a.
    /chooseDefault.

:The creator captures two strings and returns a zero-argument verb:
v/v/s/makeDefault } s/a s/b }
    v/s/getDefault }
        if zl s/a s/b s/a.
    /getDefault.


:This creator captures a fallback; the returned verb accepts two candidates:
v/v/s/makeDefault s/a s/b } s/fallback }
    v/s/chooseDefault s/a s/b }
        if zl s/a
            if zl s/b s/fallback s/b
            s/a.
    /chooseDefault.

:These are alternative definitions of makeDefault, not overloads.


v/l/u32/appendU32 l/u32/a l/u32/b
    test works
        in l/u32: u32:0 u32:1 } l/u32: u32:2 u32:3 }
        out l/u32: u32:0 u32:1 u32:2 u32:3 }
    concat l/u32/a l/u32/b.

v/s/getEnvCodeLanguage } unimplemented s:"Environment language".

v/s/getTargetLanguageForDctCodeToText
    new s/targetLanguage getFormatImportSetting s:"codetotext" s:"language".
    if zl s/targetLanguage getEnvCodeLanguage s/targetLanguage.

: OPEN: Define ELAD decoding and malformed-input errors.
v/l/dc/dcaFromElad s/in } unimplemented s:"ELAD decoding".

v/l/dc/push l/dc/in dc/toPush
    concat l/dc/in l/dc: dc/toPush }.

: OPEN: Missing mappings should be option/s; empty text may be a valid mapping.
v/l/dc/convertElementAndAppend dc/e s/targetLanguage l/dc/converted
    new s/temp dcGetMappingToFormat dc/e s/targetLanguage.
    if ne u64:0 len s/temp
        concat l/dc/converted dcaFromElad s/temp
        push l/dc/converted dc/e.

: OPEN: This returns Dc values, not s or dcs; define the intended text conversion.
v/l/dc/dctCodeToText l/dc/in
    new l/dc/res l/dc: }.
    new s/targetLanguage getTargetLanguageForDctCodeToText.
    foreach l/dc/in do
        set l/dc/res convertElementAndAppend dc/this s/targetLanguage l/dc/res.
    }.
    l/dc/res.